1
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:05,940
A TRIP ON THE TRUE NORTH

2
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:12,520
Li Dayu and her cousin Liu Qian were on a trip to Canada to visit their cousins in Montreal

3
00:00:12,520 --> 00:00:13,880
on the Atlantic coast.

4
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:16,920
Rather than take the aeroplane all the way,

5
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:22,780
they decided to fly to Vancouver and then take the train west to east across Canada.

6
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:26,680
The thought that they could cross the whole continent was exciting.

7
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:30,860
Their friend, Danny Lin, was waiting at the airport.

8
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,860
On the way to the station, he chatted about their trip.

9
00:00:41,340 --> 00:00:43,480
You’re going to see some great scenery.

10
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:47,480
Going eastward, you’ll pass mountains and thousands of lakes

11
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:50,940
and forests, as well as wide rivers and large cities.

12
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:07,100
Here in Vancouver, you’re in Canada’s warmest part.

13
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:10,160
People say it is Canada’s most beautiful city,

14
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:13,340
surrounded by mountains and the Pacific Ocean.

15
00:01:21,980 --> 00:01:24,020
Its population is increasing rapidly.

16
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:47,000
Earlier that day, when they crossed the Rocky Mountains,

17
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:51,500
they managed to catch sight of some mountain goats and even a grizzly bear

18
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:52,560
and an eagle.

19
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:57,100
Their next stop was Calgary, which is famous for the Calgary Stampede.

20
00:01:58,060 --> 00:02:00,940
Cowboys from all over the world come to compete in the Stampede.

21
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:07,480
Many of them have a gift for riding wild horses and can win thousands of dollars in prizes.

22
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:13,020
After two days’ travel, the girls began to realize that Canada is quite empty.

23
00:02:33,980 --> 00:02:36,660
After dinner, they were back in an urban area,

24
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:40,440
the busy port city of Thunder Bay at the top of the Great Lakes.

25
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:45,740
The girls were surprised at the fact that ocean ships can sail up the Great Lakes.

26
00:02:46,780 --> 00:02:49,040
Because of the Great Lakes, they learned,

27
00:02:49,260 --> 00:02:53,180
Canada has more fresh water than any other country in the world.

28
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:57,640
In fact, it has one-third of the world’s total fresh water,

29
00:02:57,640 --> 00:03:00,120
and much of it is in the Great Lakes.
